course: dictionary
lesson: 6338
title: Who is a mourner?
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A mourner is a person who feels or shows sadness because someone has died. Mourners are often found at a funeral, the event where people say goodbye. The words around the word give you the clues: «Mourners» at a funeral, in dark clothes, laying flowers.
explain: Mourners show their sadness in different ways, and families in different places do it differently. In Ireland, «a wake is often held at home», where people visit, pray, chat and share food. Mourners there say «sorry for your trouble» to the family.
explain: Jewish families «sit shiva», which means a week of mourning at home, when friends visit with food and comfort. Mourners say the Kaddish, a prayer praising God. The word mourner is linked to mourn, mourning and grief, so these words all belong to the same family of meaning.
fact: A mourner is a person who feels or shows sadness because someone has died.
fact: Mourners are often at a funeral, where they may wear dark clothes and lay flowers.
fact: Mourn, mourning and grief are linked words. Each one is about sadness after a death.
fact: «Sit shiva» means a week of mourning at home, when friends visit with food and comfort.
fact: The Kaddish is a prayer praising God, and mourners often say it.
exercise: «Mourners wore dark clothes at the funeral.» What is a mourner? | A person who sings at a party | A person who is cross about the weather | A person who sells flowers in the market | *A person who feels or shows sadness because someone has died
exercise: In Ireland, mourners say «sorry for your trouble». What are they showing? | Shouting at the family for being sad | Telling a joke to cheer the family up | A wish to leave early | *Sympathy for a family who has lost someone
exercise: «Jewish families «sit shiva», a week of mourning at home.» What does mourning mean? | Dancing and singing at a party | Cooking a big dinner for the family | *Showing deep sadness after someone has died | Going back to school
test: Mourn is a word linked to mourner. Which other word is linked to it? | *Grief | Carrot | Sunshine
test: Why might a mourner wear dark clothes? | *To show sadness at a funeral | To be seen easily in the dark | To keep warm in the rain | To look like a film star
exam: Which description fits a mourner best? | *A person who feels sad because someone has died | A driver who fixes cars | A teacher who marks homework | A cheerful guest at a birthday party
